--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
What this is not
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

These are not OSI-approved open source licenses. They restrict who may use the
software commercially, which an open source license may not do. Practically:
GitHub will not label this repository as open source, the code cannot be
combined with GPL-licensed code, and some people will decline to contribute to
a project they cannot use commercially. That is the cost of the large-company
restriction, and it is deliberate.

